file C:\Users\dalbrecht\Research
    Projects\ManyDaughters\ManyDaughters_DataPreprocessing/data/derived_confi
    > dential/5%-sample/h2_dataset.dta saved

. 
. 
. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
. * FILTERS * (Please adapt according to your needs)
.         
.         * Only keep participants from private households
.         keep if inlist(pop,1,2)
(4,698 observations deleted)

.         
.         keep cid pid hid syear gebjahr pop pld0026 plh0004

.         
.         * only keep people 18 and older
.         drop if syear - gebjahr < 18
(2,636 observations deleted)

.         
. 
. * GENERATE VARIABLES * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * create indicators for having daugthers
.         gen has_daughters = .
(27,894 missing values generated)

.         replace has_daughters = 0 if pld0026 == -2
(2,403 real changes made)

.         replace has_daughters = 1 if pld0026 > 0
(3,765 real changes made)

.         
.         * carry forward daugher indicator
.         sort pid syear

.         by pid: gen d_filled = has_daughters
(21,726 missing values generated)

.         by pid: replace d_filled = d_filled[_n-1] if missing(d_filled)
(15414 real changes made)

.         drop has_daughters

.         rename d_filled has_daughters

. 
.         * clean plh0004 political attitude
.         gen clean_plh0004 = .
(27,894 missing values generated)

.         replace clean_plh0004 = plh0004 if plh0004 != . & plh0004 >= 0
(4,520 real changes made)

.         
.         * only keep first row where both are non-missing
.         egen first_both_year = min(cond(!missing(clean_plh0004) & !missing(ha
> s_daughters), syear, .)), by(pid)
(7,259 missing values generated)

.         keep if syear == first_both_year
(26,122 observations deleted)

.         drop first_both_year

.         
.         * reverse coding
.         gen h2_dep_var = 10 - clean_plh0004

. 
.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * Standard OLS regression with robust standard errors. We regress the
>  main dependent variable on an indicator variable for having at least one dau
> ghter.
. 
.         reg h2_dep_var has_daughters, vce(robust)

Linear regression                               Number of obs     =      1,772
                                                F(1, 1770)        =       1.48
                                                Prob > F          =     0.2246
                                                R-squared         =     0.0008
                                                Root MSE          =     1.7269

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
             |               Robust
  h2_dep_var | Coefficient  std. err.      t    P>|t|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
has_daught~s |   .0998939   .0822253     1.21   0.225    -.0613751    .2611628
       _cons |   5.222342    .056143    93.02   0.000     5.112228    5.332455
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. 
. 
. * EXTRACT AND EXPORT RESULTS * (Please check whether the suggested code autom
> atically picks up the correct statistics for your chosen regression analysis 
> and adapt if needed)
. 
.         * Extract the required statistics
. 
.                 * (i) coefficient estimate
.                 local coefficient = _b[has_daughters]

. 
.                 * (ii) standard error
.                 local se = _se[has_daughters]

. 
.                 * (iii) family of the test statistic (e.g. z, t, F, Chi²)
.                 local test_stat_family = "t"

. 
.                 * (iv) residual and model degrees of freedom (DFs) if applica
> ble
.                 local df_residual = e(df_r)

.                 local df_model = e(df_m)

. 
.                 * (v) p-value
.                 local p_value = _b[has_daughters] / _se[has_daughters]

.                 local p_value = 2 * ttail(e(df_r), abs(`p_value'))

. 
.                 * (vi) number of observations
.                 local num_obs = e(N)

. 
.                 * (vii) number of participants
.                 quietly levelsof pid if e(sample), local(participants)

.                 local num_participants : word count `participants'

. 
.                 * (viii) interpretation of directionality
.                 scalar coef_d_daughter = _b[has_daughters]

.                 local interpretation "positive coefficient is in line with hy
> pothesis"

. 
